# terminal-shell-mini

Tiny GPT-2-style model that imitates Ubuntu 22.04 bash output and answers short questions about a session.

| | |
| --- | --- |
| Parameters | __PARAMS__ |
| Git SHA | `__GIT_SHA__` |
| Tokenizer | `gpt2` plus chat marker tokens |
| Training | GitHub Actions CPU runner, `ml/config/tiny.yaml` |
| Data | Synthetic `ubuntu:22.04` sessions from `ml/data/generate_sessions.py` |

## Prompt format

```
<|system|>
You are a Linux terminal on Ubuntu. ...
<|user|>
user@dev:~$ pwd
<|assistant|>
/home/user
<|end|>
```

The local server in `serve/` turns OpenAI `messages` into this prompt.

## Intended use

A toy terminal for `terminal-gpt` pointed at `POST /v1/chat/completions`. It is not a real shell, and it is not a general chatbot.

## How this checkpoint was published

GitHub Actions workflow `ML train` uploaded this folder with `HF_TOKEN`. The git SHA above is the commit that produced the weights.
